[media]","[""Hello  , the PR has been sent and built successfully locally. For the variable 'timer' at:
{quote}
 this.timer.scheduleAtFixedRate(task, delay, intervalDuration);
} else{
 EJB3_TIMER_LOGGER.debugv(""Scheduling a single action timer {0}
starting at {1} milliseconds from now"", timer, delay);
// if in past, then trigger immediately; if overdue by 5 minutes, set next expiration to current time
if (delay < 0) {
  if (delay < -300000) {
     timer.nextExpiration = new Date(currentTime);
    }
 delay = 0;
 }
this.timer.schedule(task, delay);
}
{quote}
I was getting a 'Cannot Find Symbol' Compilation Error. So, I have used the following instead. Please review.
{quote}
  this.timerInjectedValue.getValue().scheduleAtFixedRate(task, delay, intervalDuration);
} else {
 EJB3_TIMER_LOGGER.debugv(""Scheduling a single action timer {0}
starting at {1} milliseconds from now"", timer, delay);
// if in past, then trigger immediately; if overdue by 5 minutes, set next expiration to current time
if (delay < 0) {
  if (delay < -300000) {
     timer.nextExpiration = new Date(currentTime);
    }
 delay = 0;
 }
this.timerInjectedValue.getValue().schedule(task, delay);
}
{quote}"", ""Verified with EAP 7.4.8.GA-CR1."", ""As all verified issues should change to closed status, closing them with the bulk update.""]"

,[""hi [~szetszwo], could you help take a look at this problem, thank you in advance!"", ""[~liuyaolong], the commitIndex is not advancing.  Was the Raft group working fine?   As you mentioned the log index [199,839,671] is much larger than the commitIndex [1,433,240].  How did the group can run like this?  Did it have 198,406,431 pending requests?
"", ""[~szetszwo] This problem also occurred before, but it is not stable to reproduce. The cluster is working normally, and should not be so many pending requests. I suspect that there exists bug in some places that causes the error. Is there any way we can troubleshoot this problem? "", ""> The cluster is working normally,  ...

[~liuyaolong], does it mean that the cluster is working for everything except for setConfiguration?

If yes, the problem may be in LeaderStateImpl.stagingState -- it somehow was not cleared up."", ""[~szetszwo] I just observed that the Alluxio master cluster handles rpc requests normally, there is no HA switchover, and there is no pending rpc request. I have observed the value of LeaderStateImpl.stagingState through arthas, it returns false, which is as expected. "", ""[~liuyaolong], since we suspect that isConfCommitted() returning false.  Would you be able to observe the values of getLog().getLastCommittedIndex() and getRaftConf().getLogEntryIndex() through arthas?
{code}
//ServerState.java
  boolean isConfCommitted() {
    return getLog().getLastCommittedIndex() >= getRaftConf().getLogEntryIndex();
  }
{code}
"", ""[~szetszwo] Yean, I have observed the values as follows:


{code:java}
[arthas@262]$ watch org.apache.ratis.server.raftlog.RaftLogBase getLastCommittedIndex '{returnObj}'
Press Q or Ctrl+C to abort.
method=org.apache.ratis.server.raftlog.RaftLogBase.getLastCommittedIndex location=AtExit
