Create a new table with the desired column names and comments and migrate the data","[""[~allen.herrera]
After increasing the length 3x, the commands works 
{code:java}
MariaDB [test]> ALTER TABLE t1 CHANGE COLUMN name1 firstname char(30);
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.080 sec)
Records: 0  Duplicates: 0  Warnings: 0

MariaDB [test]> ALTER TABLE t1 CHANGE COLUMN firstname firstname char(30) COMMENT 'new comment';
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.077 sec)
Records: 0  Duplicates: 0  Warnings: 0

MariaDB [test]> ALTER TABLE t1 CHANGE COLUMN name2 lastname varchar(300);
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.085 sec)
Records: 0  Duplicates: 0  Warnings: 0

MariaDB [test]> ALTER TABLE t1 CHANGE COLUMN lastname lastname  varchar(300) COMMENT 'new comment';
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.079 sec)
Records: 0  Duplicates: 0  Warnings: 0
{code}
